WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.263
For each attribute both systems
write, the check assigns a severity.

2
00:00:04.263 --> 00:00:05.980
Both update it: a Finding,

3
00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:10.188
because each overwrites the
other and drift never settles.

4
00:00:10.188 --> 00:00:13.313
One updates it and the
other sets it at creation:

5
00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:16.038
a Warning, two sources
for its first value.

6
00:00:16.038 --> 00:00:18.738
Both set it only at creation: Info.

7
00:00:18.738 --> 00:00:20.738
Any Finding fails the command.

8
00:00:20.738 --> 00:00:23.824
Names are matched ignoring
case, and an alias maps a

9
00:00:23.824 --> 00:00:27.350
SailPoint field to its Entra
attribute where they differ.

10
00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:32.260
The check never guesses that mapping;
the alias list is a reviewed input.
